 rew-comedy-of-errors-and-twelfth-night-in-repertory
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Arsenic and Old Lace
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260830T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260830T163000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-1377@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Kesselring's black comedy: two sweet aunts\, a body in the win
 dow seat\, and elderberry wine best declined.\n\nJoseph Kesselring's 1941 
 farce\, later the Frank Capra film with Cary Grant. Drama critic Mortimer 
 Brewster is about to announce his engagement when he finds a corpse in his
  elderly aunts' window seat\, and the ladies are entirely unbothered by it
 . Their elderberry wine\, it turns out\, carries more than a hint of arsen
 ic. Also in the house: a brother convinced he is Teddy Roosevelt and a fug
 itive sibling with a face rebuilt by a shady plastic surgeon. From the Hen
 ry Players\, a volunteer community theatre company.
GEO:33.4486439;-84.1418279
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050010Z
LOCATION:The Henry Players Theater\, 136 Hood St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/arsenic-and-old-lace-tickets-271699
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:On Golden Pond
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260830T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260830T173000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-707@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Ernest Thompson's comedy-drama of a long marriage\, a prickly 
 father-daughter reunion\, and one Maine summer.\n\nErnest Thompson's play 
 about Ethel and Norman Thayer\, spending their 48th summer at their lake h
 ouse in the Maine woods as Norman turns 80 and his memory starts slipping 
 into cantankerously morbid jokes. The birthday brings their daughter Chels
 ea\, her boyfriend\, and his teenage son\, stirring up old grievances betw
 een father and daughter while Norman finds an unexpected fishing partner i
 n the boy. Best known from the 1981 film with Henry Fonda and Katharine He
 pburn. From Players Guild at Sugar Hill.
GEO:34.1070667;-84.0353528
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050020Z
LOCATION:The Eagle Theater\, 5029 W Broad St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/36627/performance/11797885/selecttickets
END:VEVENT
