BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THE PILLOWMAN
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T220000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-8456@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Martin McDonagh's pitch-black thriller: a writer interrogated 
 when child murders start mirroring his grim fairy tales.\n\nMartin McDonag
 h's 2003 play follows Katurian\, a writer of gruesome fairy tales living u
 nder a police state\, hauled in for questioning when a string of child mur
 ders looks suspiciously like his fiction. Two detectives run a good cop/ba
 d cop interrogation while the line between the stories and the crimes keep
 s dissolving. It is McDonagh at his most extreme — very funny and genuin
 ely disturbing\, often in the same beat — and it won the Olivier Award f
 or Best New Play. Produced by Out of Box Theatre.
GEO:33.9148699;-84.3601692
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050018Z
LOCATION:Out of Box Theatre\, 585 Cobb Pkwy SE\, Suite G-1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/the-pillowman-3
END:VEVENT
