BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:i never asked for a gofundme
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T193000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-35@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:A world-premiere play: top surgery mistaken for breast cancer\
 , and a small-town GoFundMe nobody asked for.\n\nMillie and her partner Av
 ery are riding out Avery's recovery from gender-affirming top surgery in M
 illie's hometown of Mobile\, Alabama. Then a nosy evangelical family frien
 d misreads the surgery as a breast-cancer fight and launches a GoFundMe on
  the couple's behalf\, making them the talk of the town and the recipients
  of donations they never wanted. Whether to keep the money\, and what keep
 ing it would cost them\, is the question. A world premiere from Actor's Ex
 press.
GEO:33.7817253;-84.4160629
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T045843Z
LOCATION:King Plow Arts Center\, 887 W Marietta St NW\, Suite J-107
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://purchase.actors-express.com/EventAvailability?EventId=32801
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T220000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-999@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:August Wilson's Pulitzer winner: a former Negro League star in
  1950s Pittsburgh\, at war with his son's dreams.\n\nAugust Wilson's 1985 
 drama\, sixth in his ten-play Pittsburgh Cycle and winner of the Pulitzer 
 Prize and the Tony for Best Play. Troy Maxson was a Negro League baseball 
 star before the color barrier broke\; now he hauls trash\, builds a fence 
 in his yard\, and refuses to let his son chase a college football scholars
 hip\, convinced the game will break the boy the way it broke him. Theatric
 al Outfit produces in partnership with Dominion Entertainment Group and th
 e Alabama Shakespeare Festival\, a two-state revival of the play.
GEO:33.757035;-84.389486
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050031Z
LOCATION:Theatrical Outfit\, 84 Luckie St NW
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THE PILLOWMAN
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T220000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-8459@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Martin McDonagh's pitch-black thriller: a writer interrogated 
 when child murders start mirroring his grim fairy tales.\n\nMartin McDonag
 h's 2003 play follows Katurian\, a writer of gruesome fairy tales living u
 nder a police state\, hauled in for questioning when a string of child mur
 ders looks suspiciously like his fiction. Two detectives run a good cop/ba
 d cop interrogation while the line between the stories and the crimes keep
 s dissolving. It is McDonagh at his most extreme — very funny and genuin
 ely disturbing\, often in the same beat — and it won the Olivier Award f
 or Best New Play. Produced by Out of Box Theatre.
GEO:33.9148699;-84.3601692
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050018Z
LOCATION:Out of Box Theatre\, 585 Cobb Pkwy SE\, Suite G-1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/the-pillowman-3
END:VEVENT
