BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweat
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270205T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270205T213000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-1390@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Lynn Nottage's Pulitzer-winning drama of factory friends in a 
 Rust Belt bar as the layoffs begin.\n\nLynn Nottage's 2015 drama\, winner 
 of the 2017 Pulitzer Prize\, set mostly in a bar in Reading\, Pennsylvania
 \, where a circle of steel-plant workers has gathered for years. When one 
 of the friends is promoted to management and jobs start moving to Mexico\,
  the lines between labor and boss\, and along race\, begin to cut through 
 the group. Nottage built the play from years of interviews with residents 
 of Reading\, then one of the poorest cities in America. From the Henry Pla
 yers.
GEO:33.4486439;-84.1418279
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050011Z
LOCATION:The Henry Players Theater\, 136 Hood St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/sweat-tickets-271676
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Women
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270205T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270205T223000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-720@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Alcott's four March sisters grow up\, in Thomas Hischak's stag
 e adaptation from Players Guild at Sugar Hill.\n\nLouisa May Alcott's nove
 l of the four March sisters — headstrong Jo\, practical Meg\, gentle Bet
 h\, and ambitious Amy — coming of age in Civil War-era New England\, eac
 h chasing a different idea of what her life should be. Thomas Hischak's st
 age adaptation\, from Players Guild at Sugar Hill.
GEO:34.1070667;-84.0353528
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T050020Z
LOCATION:The Eagle Theater\, 5029 W Broad St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/36627/performance/11797894/selecttickets
END:VEVENT
