DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270403T213000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-1296@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Tennessee Williams' 1947 tragedy of Blanche DuBois\, her illus
 ions\, and the brother-in-law who sees through them.\n\nTennessee Williams
 ' 1947 drama\, still one of the towering American plays. After losing the 
 family home to creditors\, Blanche DuBois arrives in a cramped New Orleans
  apartment to live with her sister Stella and a brother-in-law\, Stanley K
 owalski\, who has no patience for her airs or her illusions. A flicker of 
 hope appears in Stanley's courtly friend Mitch\, but Blanche's past keeps 
 circling closer. From Arcadia Theater\, Alpharetta's community company.
GEO:34.0765277;-84.2884766
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730T045847Z
LOCATION:Arcadia Theater\, 180 Academy St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/a-streetcar-named-desire-tickets-279868
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lauren Gunderson's The Book of Will
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270403T193000
DTSTAMP:20260730T153943Z
UID:occ-1543@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Gunderson's true story of the two actors who saved half of Sha
 kespeare's plays by printing the First Folio.\n\nAfter Shakespeare's death
 \, his fellow actors Henry Condell and John Heminges set out to collect an
 d publish his plays as the First Folio\, without which roughly half of the
 m would have vanished. Lauren Gunderson\, the Atlanta-born writer who has 
 repeatedly topped American Theatre's list of the country's most-produced l
 iving playwrights\, spins the history into a story of friendship\, grief\,
  and stubborn devotion to the words. From the Atlanta Shakespeare Company\
 , performed with the tavern's table seating and food and drink service.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T204412Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/lauren-gundersons-t
 he-book-of-will
END:VEVENT
